The Qatar Financial Markets Authority (QFMA) oversees governance for listed companies.
Board of Directors & Shareholder Rights:
Companies must ensure board diversity and independent representation.
Minority shareholders receive additional protections, including representation rights.
Electronic voting at general assemblies is introduced.
Disclosure & Transparency:
Board members must disclose conflicts of interest and related-party transactions.
Companies must provide detailed financial statements, director remuneration reports, and donation disclosures.
Anti-Corruption & Fair Business Practices:
Board members and executives cannot engage in business that competes with their company without prior approval.
Companies must disclose transactions exceeding 10% of their net assets.
Regulatory Oversight & Enforcement:
Stricter penalties for non-compliance, including fines and disqualification of board members.
Strengthened AML/CFT (Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing) requirements.
These amendments improve corporate accountability, financial integrity, and investor protection in Qatar’s business environment.', 'Qatar', 'climate', 'in_force', '2021-01-01'::date, 'Qatar', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/148_2', ARRAY['sdg2', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'sdg9', 'qatar']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('16889924-ea99-5fd0-bfe3-399f02cf2bce', 'Qatar Governance Code for Companies & Legal Entities Listed', 'Governance Code for Companies & Legal Entities Listed on the Main Market (QFMA, 2016)', 'Issued by the Qatar Financial Markets Authority (QFMA) under Decision No. (5) of 2016, this Governance Code establishes corporate governance best practices for listed companies and legal entities in Qatar’s financial markets. It aims to enhance transparency, board accountability, shareholder rights, and corporate social responsibility.

Key provisions include:

Board of Directors Responsibilities:
Companies must have independent and non-executive board members.
The Chairman cannot hold an executive role.
Transparency & Disclosure:
Companies must disclose financial statements, board decisions, and conflicts of interest.
Related-party transactions must be approved by shareholders.
Shareholder Rights & Protections:
Shareholders have equal voting rights, access to corporate information, and participation in general assemblies.
Minority shareholders are protected from majority control.
Internal & External Audits:
Companies must have internal control systems and independent external auditors.
Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR):
Companies must adopt ESG and sustainability measures.
The Code aligns with international corporate governance frameworks, including OECD, G20, and GCC governance principles.', 'Issued by the Qatar Financial Markets Authority (QFMA) under Decision No. (5) of 2016, this Governance Code establishes corporate governance best practices for listed companies and legal entities in Qatar’s financial markets. It aims to enhance transparency, board accountability, shareholder rights, and corporate social responsibility.

Key provisions include:

Board of Directors Responsibilities:
Companies must have independent and non-executive board members.
The Chairman cannot hold an executive role.
Transparency & Disclosure:
Companies must disclose financial statements, board decisions, and conflicts of interest.
Related-party transactions must be approved by shareholders.
Shareholder Rights & Protections:
Shareholders have equal voting rights, access to corporate information, and participation in general assemblies.
Minority shareholders are protected from majority control.
Internal & External Audits:
Companies must have internal control systems and independent external auditors.
Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR):
Companies must adopt ESG and sustainability measures.
The Code aligns with international corporate governance frameworks, including OECD, G20, and GCC governance principles.', 'Issued by the Qatar Financial Markets Authority (QFMA) under Decision No. (5) of 2016, this Governance Code establishes corporate governance best practices for listed companies and legal entities in Qatar’s financial markets. It aims to enhance transparency, board accountability, shareholder rights, and corporate social responsibility.

Key provisions include:

Board of Directors Responsibilities:
Companies must have independent and non-executive board members.
The Chairman cannot hold an executive role.
Transparency & Disclosure:
Companies must disclose financial statements, board decisions, and conflicts of interest.
Related-party transactions must be approved by shareholders.
Shareholder Rights & Protections:
