Minority shareholders are protected from majority control.
Internal & External Audits:
Companies must have internal control systems and independent external auditors.
Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR):
Companies must adopt ESG and sustainability measures.
The Code aligns with international corporate governance frameworks, including OECD, G20, and GCC governance principles.', 'Qatar', 'climate', 'in_force', '2016-01-01'::date, 'Qatar', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/148_3', ARRAY['sdg2', 'other sustainability policy', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'sdg9', 'qatar']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('b240f00b-c5b4-55a8-a0fb-367327e25c07', 'Qatar Governance Code for Companies & Legal Entities Listed', 'Governance Code for Companies & Legal Entities Listed on the Main Market', 'QFMA developed this code to promote the practice of corporate governance, transparency, stakeholder/shareholder engagement, etc. This Code shall apply to companies, legal entities listed on the main Market unless there is a special provision on this regard stipulated in any of the Authority’s Legislations.', 'QFMA developed this code to promote the practice of corporate governance, transparency, stakeholder/shareholder engagement, etc. This Code shall apply to companies, legal entities listed on the main Market unless there is a special provision on this regard stipulated in any of the Authority’s Legislations.', 'QFMA developed this code to promote the practice of corporate governance, transparency, stakeholder/shareholder engagement, etc. This Code shall apply to companies, legal entities listed on the main Market unless there is a special provision on this regard stipulated in any of the Authority’s Legislations.', 'Qatar', 'governance', 'in_force', '2016-01-01'::date, 'Qatar', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/148_4', ARRAY['regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'qatar']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('66534f56-30f4-5b68-9cc4-92cd0d51d748', 'Qatar Corporate Governance Code for Companies Listed on the', 'Corporate Governance Code for Companies Listed on the Venture Market', 'This Code comprises principles and practices to improve the governance system especially at the Board level, which is a prerequisite for improving the performance of any company. The CG Code has been drafted with taking into account the best international practices for Corporate Governance, including but not limited to those developed by the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), the Bank for International Settlements (BIS), the International Corporate Governance Network (ICGN) and the International Institute of Finance (IIF), adapting those provisions to the applicable laws in the State of Qatar, including the Commercial Companies Law and Securities Market Regulations.', 'This Code comprises principles and practices to improve the governance system especially at the Board level, which is a prerequisite for improving the performance of any company. The CG Code has been drafted with taking into account the best international practices for Corporate Governance, including but not limited to those developed by the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), the Bank for International Settlements (BIS), the International Corporate Governance Network (ICGN) and the International Institute of Finance (IIF), adapting those provisions to the applicable laws in the State of Qatar, including the Commercial Companies Law and Securities Market Regulations.', 'This Code comprises principles and practices to improve the governance system especially at the Board level, which is a prerequisite for improving the performance of any company. The CG Code has been drafted with taking into account the best international practices for Corporate Governance, including but not limited to those developed by the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), the Bank for International Settlements (BIS), the International Corporate Governance Network (ICGN) and the International Institute of Finance (IIF), adapting those provisions to the applicable laws in the State of Qatar, including the Commercial Companies Law and Securities Market Regulations.', 'Qatar', 'governance', 'in_force', '2016-01-01'::date, 'Qatar', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/148_6', ARRAY['regulations', 'sdg11', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'qatar']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('bf195c7f-008f-51af-83b2-9de30ac8513f', 'Qatar Corporate Governance Principles for Banks', 'Corporate Governance Principles for Banks', 'Corporate governance for banks is of a great importance to both the supervisory authorities and international and regional organizations as well. A set of international publications have been issued on the standards and guidelines on corporate governance for banks. Considering its importance and significance to the financial sector, corporate governance guidelines and standards are adopted by supervisory authorities. Most known relevant publications are those issued by Basel Committee on Corporate Governance principles for banks, and publication issued by the (OECD). It is worth mentioning that QCB has issued guidelines on corporate governance in Instructions to Banks book, and guidelines on corporate governance for financial institutions in 2008. In view of the recent regulatory and international requirements and publications following the financial crisis, more responsibilities and wider role have been assigned to banks by regulators and all stakeholders. As such QCB is issuing a revised version of corporate governance principles including recent update thereof.', 'Corporate governance for banks is of a great importance to both the supervisory authorities and international and regional organizations as well. A set of international publications have been issued on the standards and guidelines on corporate governance for banks. Considering its importance and significance to the financial sector, corporate governance guidelines and standards are adopted by supervisory authorities. Most known relevant publications are those issued by Basel Committee on Corporate Governance principles for banks, and publication issued by the (OECD). It is worth mentioning that QCB has issued guidelines on corporate governance in Instructions to Banks book, and guidelines on corporate governance for financial institutions in 2008. In view of the recent regulatory and international requirements and publications following the financial crisis, more responsibilities and wider role have been assigned to banks by regulators and all stakeholders. As such QCB is issuing a revised version of corporate governance principles including recent update thereof.', 'Corporate governance for banks is of a great importance to both the supervisory authorities and international and regional organizations as well. A set of international publications have been issued on the standards and guidelines on corporate governance for banks. Considering its importance and significance to the financial sector, corporate governance guidelines and standards are adopted by supervisory authorities. Most known relevant publications are those issued by Basel Committee on Corporate Governance principles for banks, and publication issued by the (OECD). It is worth mentioning that QCB has issued guidelines on corporate governance in Instructions to Banks book, and guidelines on corporate governance for financial institutions in 2008. In view of the recent regulatory and international requirements and publications following the financial crisis, more responsibilities and wider role have been assigned to banks by regulators and all stakeholders. As such QCB is issuing a revised version of corporate governance principles including recent update thereof.', 'Qatar', 'climate', 'in_force', '2015-01-01'::date, 'Qatar', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/148_5', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'qatar', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'voluntary']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('95eb2475-9679-5c40-9f34-798ed7139e37', 'Qatar Translation of the Corporate Governance Code for Companies', 'Translation of the Corporate Governance Code for Companies Listed in Markets Regulated by the Qatar Financial Markets Authority', 'This Corporate Governance Code has been developed for Joint Stock Companies listed on any stock market that is subject to the regulation of the Qatar Financial Markets Authority (the CG Code, or this Code). This Code comprises principles and practices to improve the quality of governance especially at the Board level. This is a prerequisite for improving the performance of any company.', 'This Corporate Governance Code has been developed for Joint Stock Companies listed on any stock market that is subject to the regulation of the Qatar Financial Markets Authority (the CG Code, or this Code). This Code comprises principles and practices to improve the quality of governance especially at the Board level. This is a prerequisite for improving the performance of any company.', 'This Corporate Governance Code has been developed for Joint Stock Companies listed on any stock market that is subject to the regulation of the Qatar Financial Markets Authority (the CG Code, or this Code). This Code comprises principles and practices to improve the quality of governance especially at the Board level. This is a prerequisite for improving the performance of any company.', 'Qatar', 'governance', 'in_force', '2009-01-01'::date, 'Qatar', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/148_1', ARRAY['regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'qatar']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('ccb4da95-d43d-537f-97c5-b175c88cbabd', 'Romania Order of the Minister of Finance nr', 'Order of the Minister of Finance nr.1421/2025 regarding the dates from which certain sustainability reporting requirements apply', 'The Order of the Minister of Finance nr. 1421/2025 establishes the dates from which certain sustainability reporting requirements will apply in Romania. It amends existing accounting regulations to incorporate the EU Directive 2025/794, which mandates member states to implement specific sustainability reporting and due diligence requirements. This policy applies to all companies subject to these accounting regulations and sets the compliance date to January 1, 2027. The requirements are mandatory for the affected entities.', 'The Order of the Minister of Finance nr. 1421/2025 establishes the dates from which certain sustainability reporting requirements will apply in Romania. It amends existing accounting regulations to incorporate the EU Directive 2025/794, which mandates member states to implement specific sustainability reporting and due diligence requirements. This policy applies to all companies subject to these accounting regulations and sets the compliance date to January 1, 2027. The requirements are mandatory for the affected entities.', 'The Order of the Minister of Finance nr. 1421/2025 establishes the dates from which certain sustainability reporting requirements will apply in Romania. It amends existing accounting regulations to incorporate the EU Directive 2025/794, which mandates member states to implement specific sustainability reporting and due diligence requirements. This policy applies to all companies subject to these accounting regulations and sets the compliance date to January 1, 2027. The requirements are mandatory for the affected entities.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2025-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_30', ARRAY['sdg13', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('91fca3d9-706a-5229-b94c-31f3953d1690', 'Romania Order of January 12, 2024 on regulating issues', 'Order No. 85 of January 12, 2024 on regulating issues related to sustainability reporting', 'Order No. 85 of January 12, 2024 in Romania focuses on regulating sustainability reporting. It amends accounting regulations to align with EU Directive 2022/2.464, emphasizing reporting on sustainability aspects for entities. The policy targets entities reporting financial statements and aims to enhance understanding of sustainability impacts and strategies.', 'Order No. 85 of January 12, 2024 in Romania focuses on regulating sustainability reporting. It amends accounting regulations to align with EU Directive 2022/2.464, emphasizing reporting on sustainability aspects for entities. The policy targets entities reporting financial statements and aims to enhance understanding of sustainability impacts and strategies.', 'Order No. 85 of January 12, 2024 in Romania focuses on regulating sustainability reporting. It amends accounting regulations to align with EU Directive 2022/2.464, emphasizing reporting on sustainability aspects for entities. The policy targets entities reporting financial statements and aims to enhance understanding of sustainability impacts and strategies.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2024-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_24', ARRAY['sdg13', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'sdg12', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('a43bfcea-791a-53e7-b557-d8345d2eff01', 'Romania Government Emergency Ordinance on financial audit activity, as', 'Government Emergency Ordinance on financial audit activity, as well as the amendment and completion of certain normative acts', 'The Government Emergency Ordinance in Romania aims to align financial audit practices with EU directives, ensuring statutory audit compliance and enhancing public trust in financial reporting. It targets auditors, audit firms, and entities subject to statutory audit requirements, emphasizing the importance of accurate financial and sustainability information.', 'The Government Emergency Ordinance in Romania aims to align financial audit practices with EU directives, ensuring statutory audit compliance and enhancing public trust in financial reporting. It targets auditors, audit firms, and entities subject to statutory audit requirements, emphasizing the importance of accurate financial and sustainability information.', 'The Government Emergency Ordinance in Romania aims to align financial audit practices with EU directives, ensuring statutory audit compliance and enhancing public trust in financial reporting. It targets auditors, audit firms, and entities subject to statutory audit requirements, emphasizing the importance of accurate financial and sustainability information.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2024-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_25', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('d4bf122c-077f-5035-a901-937f44ded3a5', 'Romania Emergency Ordinance 137 amending and supplementing Law', 'Emergency Ordinance 137 amending and supplementing Law No. 162/2017 on the statutory audit of annual financial statements and consolidated annual financial statements and amending some normative acts,', 'The Emergency Ordinance 137 in Romania amends and supplements the statutory audit law to align with EU directives on financial reporting sustainability. It aims to enhance the quality of financial information, ensure compliance with EU regulations, and improve public trust in financial reporting by auditors and firms.', 'The Emergency Ordinance 137 in Romania amends and supplements the statutory audit law to align with EU directives on financial reporting sustainability. It aims to enhance the quality of financial information, ensure compliance with EU regulations, and improve public trust in financial reporting by auditors and firms.', 'The Emergency Ordinance 137 in Romania amends and supplements the statutory audit law to align with EU directives on financial reporting sustainability. It aims to enhance the quality of financial information, ensure compliance with EU regulations, and improve public trust in financial reporting by auditors and firms.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2024-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_26', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('8dc318d3-e57c-58a0-aa4e-9fc970565214', 'Romania Financial Supervisory Authority (FSA) Norm', 'Financial Supervisory Authority (FSA) Norm No. 4/2024:', 'The Financial Supervisory Authority (FSA) Norm No. 4/2024 modifies the previous Norm No. 39/2015 regarding accounting regulations compliant with international financial reporting standards. It applies to entities authorized, regulated, and supervised by the FSA in the financial instruments and investments sector, as well as the Investor Compensation Fund. The norm introduces mandatory reporting requirements starting from the financial year 2027 for certain entities and from 2028 for others, aligning with EU Directive 2025/794 on corporate sustainability reporting. The norm is mandatory and will take effect upon publication in the Official Monitor of Romania.', 'The Financial Supervisory Authority (FSA) Norm No. 4/2024 modifies the previous Norm No. 39/2015 regarding accounting regulations compliant with international financial reporting standards. It applies to entities authorized, regulated, and supervised by the FSA in the financial instruments and investments sector, as well as the Investor Compensation Fund. The norm introduces mandatory reporting requirements starting from the financial year 2027 for certain entities and from 2028 for others, aligning with EU Directive 2025/794 on corporate sustainability reporting. The norm is mandatory and will take effect upon publication in the Official Monitor of Romania.', 'The Financial Supervisory Authority (FSA) Norm No. 4/2024 modifies the previous Norm No. 39/2015 regarding accounting regulations compliant with international financial reporting standards. It applies to entities authorized, regulated, and supervised by the FSA in the financial instruments and investments sector, as well as the Investor Compensation Fund. The norm introduces mandatory reporting requirements starting from the financial year 2027 for certain entities and from 2028 for others, aligning with EU Directive 2025/794 on corporate sustainability reporting. The norm is mandatory and will take effect upon publication in the Official Monitor of Romania.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2024-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_28', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('11acfee0-4e81-5c11-a08c-f2db54ea3801', 'National Bank of Romania (BNR) Order', 'National Bank of Romania (BNR) Order No. 1/2024:', 'The National Bank of Romania''s Order No. 1/2024 amends previous regulations to align accounting standards with the EU''s sustainability reporting directive. It applies to large entities and parent companies with over 500 employees, mandating compliance with new reporting requirements starting from the financial year 2024 for certain entities, and extending to smaller entities by 2026. This order aims to enhance transparency in financial reporting regarding sustainability practices, making it a crucial step for the banking and financial sectors in Romania.', 'The National Bank of Romania''s Order No. 1/2024 amends previous regulations to align accounting standards with the EU''s sustainability reporting directive. It applies to large entities and parent companies with over 500 employees, mandating compliance with new reporting requirements starting from the financial year 2024 for certain entities, and extending to smaller entities by 2026. This order aims to enhance transparency in financial reporting regarding sustainability practices, making it a crucial step for the banking and financial sectors in Romania.', 'The National Bank of Romania''s Order No. 1/2024 amends previous regulations to align accounting standards with the EU''s sustainability reporting directive. It applies to large entities and parent companies with over 500 employees, mandating compliance with new reporting requirements starting from the financial year 2024 for certain entities, and extending to smaller entities by 2026. This order aims to enhance transparency in financial reporting regarding sustainability practices, making it a crucial step for the banking and financial sectors in Romania.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2024-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_29', ARRAY['regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('69be0a7e-6608-5c0a-b0ed-281b12a4ffda', 'Methodology for sustainability reporting - Romanian Sustainability Code', 'Methodology for sustainability reporting - Romanian Sustainability Code 2023', 'This document presents a methodology for sustainability reporting that provides clear guidance on the content requirements and the process of preparing sustainability reports for interested entities.', 'This document presents a methodology for sustainability reporting that provides clear guidance on the content requirements and the process of preparing sustainability reports for interested entities.', 'This document presents a methodology for sustainability reporting that provides clear guidance on the content requirements and the process of preparing sustainability reports for interested entities.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2023-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_23', ARRAY['sdg13', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('daed8149-13f8-5616-b88a-bbe05b0684c5', 'Romania Law of December 29, 2023 on ensuring a', 'Law No. 431 of December 29, 2023 on ensuring a global minimum level of taxation for multinational enterprise groups and large national groups', 'Law No. 431 of December 29, 2023 in Romania establishes a global minimum taxation level for multinational and large national enterprise groups. It includes rules for income inclusion and addressing under-taxed profits. The policy applies to entities in Romania with annual group income exceeding €750 million.', 'Law No. 431 of December 29, 2023 in Romania establishes a global minimum taxation level for multinational and large national enterprise groups. It includes rules for income inclusion and addressing under-taxed profits. The policy applies to entities in Romania with annual group income exceeding €750 million.', 'Law No. 431 of December 29, 2023 in Romania establishes a global minimum taxation level for multinational and large national enterprise groups. It includes rules for income inclusion and addressing under-taxed profits. The policy applies to entities in Romania with annual group income exceeding €750 million.', 'Romania', 'social', 'in_force', '2023-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_27', ARRAY['mandatory', 'sdg10', 'regulations', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('50f5ca49-6185-56e4-b613-2cdaef6ae4f8', 'Romania Guide for Responsible Business', 'Guide for Responsible Business', 'This Guide is a tool that provides clear information about the actions that a company could implement in order to improve its sustainability performance. For clarity, the actions are structured in seven principles aligned with the most important international initiatives in the field of sustainability, such as: the Global Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), the United Nations Global Compact and the Global Reporting Initiative (GRI), as well as the requirements of some of the most relevant ESG rating agencies. To facilitate the transposition of these actions, a series of good practices identified at the national level among ARIR member companies have also been included. At the same time, the Guide is also a presentation catalogue of all founding members and associates.', 'This Guide is a tool that provides clear information about the actions that a company could implement in order to improve its sustainability performance. For clarity, the actions are structured in seven principles aligned with the most important international initiatives in the field of sustainability, such as: the Global Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), the United Nations Global Compact and the Global Reporting Initiative (GRI), as well as the requirements of some of the most relevant ESG rating agencies. To facilitate the transposition of these actions, a series of good practices identified at the national level among ARIR member companies have also been included. At the same time, the Guide is also a presentation catalogue of all founding members and associates.', 'This Guide is a tool that provides clear information about the actions that a company could implement in order to improve its sustainability performance. For clarity, the actions are structured in seven principles aligned with the most important international initiatives in the field of sustainability, such as: the Global Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), the United Nations Global Compact and the Global Reporting Initiative (GRI), as well as the requirements of some of the most relevant ESG rating agencies. To facilitate the transposition of these actions, a series of good practices identified at the national level among ARIR member companies have also been included. At the same time, the Guide is also a presentation catalogue of all founding members and associates.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2021-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_22', ARRAY['sdg13', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('84db571a-4f56-5a03-b840-ac105fb72925', 'Romania Order ,938 of August 17, 2016 regarding the', 'Order no. 1,938 of August 17, 2016 regarding the modification and completion of some accounting regulations', 'Accounting regulations in regards to the annual financial statement and consolidated financial statement are amended and supplemented by this order to include the partial transposition of the EU Directive 2014/95/EU regarding the disclosure of non-financial information. Entities with an average of 500 employees during the financial year are required to prepare a non-financial statement as part of the management report, including information in relation to environmental issues, social and personal, human rights, and combating corruption and bribery. The statement should include a brief description of the business model, a description of the policies, results, main risks and key performance indicators in relation to relevant non-financial issues. Where an entity does not implement policies in regards to non-financial issues, they must explain why.', 'Accounting regulations in regards to the annual financial statement and consolidated financial statement are amended and supplemented by this order to include the partial transposition of the EU Directive 2014/95/EU regarding the disclosure of non-financial information. Entities with an average of 500 employees during the financial year are required to prepare a non-financial statement as part of the management report, including information in relation to environmental issues, social and personal, human rights, and combating corruption and bribery. The statement should include a brief description of the business model, a description of the policies, results, main risks and key performance indicators in relation to relevant non-financial issues. Where an entity does not implement policies in regards to non-financial issues, they must explain why.', 'Accounting regulations in regards to the annual financial statement and consolidated financial statement are amended and supplemented by this order to include the partial transposition of the EU Directive 2014/95/EU regarding the disclosure of non-financial information. Entities with an average of 500 employees during the financial year are required to prepare a non-financial statement as part of the management report, including information in relation to environmental issues, social and personal, human rights, and combating corruption and bribery. The statement should include a brief description of the business model, a description of the policies, results, main risks and key performance indicators in relation to relevant non-financial issues. Where an entity does not implement policies in regards to non-financial issues, they must explain why.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2016-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_19', ARRAY['regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('0ae0a247-7bb3-5957-b543-c6f093dee350', 'Romanian Labor Code', 'Romanian Labor Code', 'This Code regulates employment relationships within the Romania. Employers and employees are obliged  to meet the standards set out within this code. This includes labor standards in relation to forced labor, equality, protection, freedom of association, working time, remuneration, health and safety, vocational training, collective bargaining, and continued social dialogue.', 'This Code regulates employment relationships within the Romania. Employers and employees are obliged  to meet the standards set out within this code. This includes labor standards in relation to forced labor, equality, protection, freedom of association, working time, remuneration, health and safety, vocational training, collective bargaining, and continued social dialogue.', 'This Code regulates employment relationships within the Romania. Employers and employees are obliged  to meet the standards set out within this code. This includes labor standards in relation to forced labor, equality, protection, freedom of association, working time, remuneration, health and safety, vocational training, collective bargaining, and continued social dialogue.', 'Romania', 'social', 'in_force', '2016-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_21', ARRAY['sdg4', 'sdg8', 'mandatory', 'mandatory_regulations', 'disclosure', 'sdg3', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('22ca50bc-ad48-5a28-9087-5a01141abe7d', 'Romania Community Investment Guide', 'Community Investment Guide', '”The Guide for Investment in the Community” comes as a continuation and supplement to the documents previously published by the American Chamber of Commerce in Romania (“The Corporate Governance Code” and “The Anti-corruption Guide”) promoting the active role and responsibility of the business sector in society. This document aims at establishing a guide that companies active in the Romanian market can utilize to define and successfully implement their policy of involvement in the community.', '”The Guide for Investment in the Community” comes as a continuation and supplement to the documents previously published by the American Chamber of Commerce in Romania (“The Corporate Governance Code” and “The Anti-corruption Guide”) promoting the active role and responsibility of the business sector in society. This document aims at establishing a guide that companies active in the Romanian market can utilize to define and successfully implement their policy of involvement in the community.', '”The Guide for Investment in the Community” comes as a continuation and supplement to the documents previously published by the American Chamber of Commerce in Romania (“The Corporate Governance Code” and “The Anti-corruption Guide”) promoting the active role and responsibility of the business sector in society. This document aims at establishing a guide that companies active in the Romanian market can utilize to define and successfully implement their policy of involvement in the community.', 'Romania', 'governance', 'in_force', '2015-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_1', ARRAY['other sustainability policy', 'regulations', 'sdg11', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('7d073bbd-be82-50ea-a396-41815ada688e', 'Romania Accounting Regulations of December 28', 'Accounting Regulations of December 28, 2015', 'These regulations implement the use of the International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS) for entities authorized, regulated and supervised by the Financial Supervisory Authority. It outlines the reporting and auditing requirements of annual financial statements, including the expected content of the management report and financial statements. Article 8 implements the EU Directive 2014/95 / EU regarding the disclosure of non-financial information. Entities with an average of 500 employees during the financial year are required to prepare a non-financial statement as part of the management report, including information in relation to environmental issues, social and personal, human rights, and combating corruption and bribery. The statement should include a brief description of the business model, a description of the policies, results, main risks and key performance indicators in relation to relevant non-financial issues. Where an entity does not implement policies in regards to non-financial issues, they must explain why.', 'These regulations implement the use of the International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS) for entities authorized, regulated and supervised by the Financial Supervisory Authority. It outlines the reporting and auditing requirements of annual financial statements, including the expected content of the management report and financial statements. Article 8 implements the EU Directive 2014/95 / EU regarding the disclosure of non-financial information. Entities with an average of 500 employees during the financial year are required to prepare a non-financial statement as part of the management report, including information in relation to environmental issues, social and personal, human rights, and combating corruption and bribery. The statement should include a brief description of the business model, a description of the policies, results, main risks and key performance indicators in relation to relevant non-financial issues. Where an entity does not implement policies in regards to non-financial issues, they must explain why.', 'These regulations implement the use of the International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS) for entities authorized, regulated and supervised by the Financial Supervisory Authority. It outlines the reporting and auditing requirements of annual financial statements, including the expected content of the management report and financial statements. Article 8 implements the EU Directive 2014/95 / EU regarding the disclosure of non-financial information. Entities with an average of 500 employees during the financial year are required to prepare a non-financial statement as part of the management report, including information in relation to environmental issues, social and personal, human rights, and combating corruption and bribery. The statement should include a brief description of the business model, a description of the policies, results, main risks and key performance indicators in relation to relevant non-financial issues. Where an entity does not implement policies in regards to non-financial issues, they must explain why.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2015-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_20', ARRAY['regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'disclosure', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('eac9d4fd-8d59-52b4-ac24-1114da1cabe5', 'Romania Rule approving the Accounting Regulations compliant with International', 'Rule No. 39/2015 approving the Accounting Regulations compliant with International Financial Reporting Standards', 'This document is concerned with rule No. 39/2015 approving the Accounting Regulations compliant with International Financial Reporting Standards, applicable to entities authorized, regulated and supervised by the Financial Supervisory Authority in the Financial Instruments and Investments Sector.', 'This document is concerned with rule No. 39/2015 approving the Accounting Regulations compliant with International Financial Reporting Standards, applicable to entities authorized, regulated and supervised by the Financial Supervisory Authority in the Financial Instruments and Investments Sector.', 'This document is concerned with rule No. 39/2015 approving the Accounting Regulations compliant with International Financial Reporting Standards, applicable to entities authorized, regulated and supervised by the Financial Supervisory Authority in the Financial Instruments and Investments Sector.', 'Romania', 'climate', 'in_force', '2015-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_3', ARRAY['regulations', 'voluntary', 'romania', 'disclosure']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('173b4c69-42f4-5c5b-8a0c-0faff38891d3', 'Romania Code of Corporate Governance', 'Code of Corporate Governance, 2015', 'This new Code replaces the original Code which was issued in 2001 and revised in 2008. The changes made to the new Code were desirable, taking into account the lessons learned from its previous ver- sions, the evolving legal environment in Romania and Europe, and the new aspirations of the society and of the stakeholders regarding the responsibilities and conduct of companies.', 'This new Code replaces the original Code which was issued in 2001 and revised in 2008. The changes made to the new Code were desirable, taking into account the lessons learned from its previous ver- sions, the evolving legal environment in Romania and Europe, and the new aspirations of the society and of the stakeholders regarding the responsibilities and conduct of companies.', 'This new Code replaces the original Code which was issued in 2001 and revised in 2008. The changes made to the new Code were desirable, taking into account the lessons learned from its previous ver- sions, the evolving legal environment in Romania and Europe, and the new aspirations of the society and of the stakeholders regarding the responsibilities and conduct of companies.', 'Romania', 'governance', 'in_force', '2015-01-01'::date, 'Romania', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/149_4', ARRAY['mandatory', 'sdg16', 'mandatory_regulations', 'disclosure', 'romania']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
